{"seq":1263,"lane":"B","class":"unhelpful-evidence","severity":"serious","evidence":"The next day she toured the Beijing robot exhibition, drawing onlookers the way her father does on his Asia trips, watching robots do flying kicks and stopping by the booths of Chinese companies built on Nvidia technology.","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §5.1 and §5.3: retain statements that help answer a research question; exclude background that does not.","mechanism":"B linked the visit to v2, NVIDIA FY2027 total revenue, without explaining how the visit changes that revenue outcome."}
{"seq":1263,"lane":"B","class":"wrong-period-link","severity":"serious","evidence":"But Jensen Huang expects it to grow ten-fold within a decade.","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §5.1: evidence must help answer the linked question; D259 permits relevant drivers but does not make an unrelated-period forecast an answer to the question.","mechanism":"B linked a decade-long physical-AI growth expectation to v72, NVIDIA FY2028 total revenue, although the passage supplies no FY2028 trajectory."}
{"seq":1270,"lane":"B","class":"unhelpful-evidence","severity":"serious","evidence":"Residents will save $15 a month because of the growth, an amount negotiated up from $8.","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §5.1 and §5.3: retain evidence that helps answer a question; exclude unrelated details.","mechanism":"B linked a local electricity-customer benefit to v4, v5 and v16, although the passage does not quantify hyperscaler spending or compute capacity."}
{"seq":1271,"lane":"judging","class":"unsupported-precision","severity":"serious","evidence":"About 3.4% year over year in December 2026: carrying forward July's 0.2% month-on-month increase implies a roughly 2.4% annualized monthly pace, and the demand restraint signal supports some easing from 3.7%; the evidence does not provide the prior-year monthly comparison needed for a precise calculation.","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §7: judgement must follow the evidence and preserve its limits.","mechanism":"The judgement selects a specific December year-over-year outcome and rung from one monthly change despite acknowledging that the prior-year monthly comparisons needed to calculate it are unavailable."}
{"seq":1273,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"inverted-revenue-ladder","severity":"blocker","evidence":"Strongly bullish: FY2026 AI-related semiconductor revenue is below $18 billion. ... Strongly bearish: FY2026 AI-related semiconductor revenue is at least $24 billion.","rule":"docs/research/2026-11-05-seven-day-request/split_seven_day_poc.py META_SYSTEM: a company ladder's labels mean good or bad for the business; docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §4 requires meaningful outcomes.","mechanism":"Record preparation reversed the business meaning of the revenue ranges. src/hivemind/extraction.py check_ladder checks label order and check_bounds checks partitioning, so the inverted meanings were written as v87."}
{"seq":1275,"lane":"B","class":"same-fact-two-homes","severity":"serious","evidence":"2026 capex $60–$64B","rule":"D207 and D259: daily evidence goes to the narrowest question; docs/DECISIONS.md §6 permits the same answer's own candidate alongside existing-question filing.","mechanism":"A and B used the same prior library: A attached this passage to new capex question v88, while B attached it to broader revenue question v79. _ledger.json records separate evidence e4432 and e4436, so the later write did not reconcile the same fact across the two outputs."}
{"seq":1277,"lane":"A","class":"unsupported-new-question","severity":"serious","evidence":"What gross margin will TSMC report for FY2026? ... The South Korean memory giant is reportedly looking to outsource some base-die production to Intel Foundry beginning with HBM4E.","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §§3–4: a new question must have independent investment significance and a source-supported reason to open it.","mechanism":"A inferred a company-wide current-year margin question from an unconfirmed potential future supplier change; the quoted evidence supplies neither a current-year margin figure nor a quantified effect on that margin."}
{"seq":1279,"lane":"matching","class":"same-passage-separate-records","severity":"serious","evidence":"As part of the expanded collaboration, MediaTek will adopt the NVIDIA NVLink Fusion™ platform to provide hyperscalers, cloud service providers and frontier model developers with a prevalidated path to develop custom XPUs and bring them into NVIDIA NVLink™-connected, rack-scale AI factories.","rule":"D248 boundary 7 and AGENTS.md §3: equal text alone does not establish identity across outlets; the same-statement exception is enabled only after its merge risks and original speaker and day are measured.","mechanism":"The two source items contain the same company announcement, but B linked seq 1278 to v2 and seq 1279 to v82. Matching returned new for both; _ledger.json contains e4442 and e4443 with different tiers. Whether cross-source merging should be enabled remains an unmeasured decision."}
{"seq":1280,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"incorrect-ladder-arithmetic","severity":"serious","evidence":"FY2027 net sales are within 5% above or below FY2026 reported net sales of $39,063,072,000. ... lo: 37009918400, hi: 41015825600.","rule":"docs/research/2026-11-05-seven-day-request/split_seven_day_poc.py META_SYSTEM: rung conditions must match their numeric bounds.","mechanism":"Record preparation's stated 5% comparison does not match its bounds: 95% and 105% of the stated reference are $37,109,918,400 and $41,016,225,600. The partition check accepts adjacent bounds without checking their arithmetic against the condition."}
{"seq":1280,"lane":"A","class":"missing-direct-financial-evidence","severity":"serious","evidence":"Years Ended June 30, ... 2026 ... Net sales ... 39,063,072","rule":"D371: track present financial information for relevant investment questions; docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §5.1: keep a question's own relevant financial figures.","mechanism":"A opened FY2027 net sales and supplied growth, demand and other passages, but did not include the filing's FY2026 net-sales figure as evidence. Record preparation used that figure as the ladder reference, leaving the reference without the corresponding cited passage."}
{"summary":{"items_read":3,"fully_read_seq":[1257,1263,1275],"not_fully_reviewed_seq":[1258,1259,1260,1261,1262,1264,1265,1266,1267,1268,1269,1270,1271,1272,1273,1274,1276,1277,1278,1279,1280],"classes":{"unhelpful-evidence":2,"wrong-period-link":1,"unsupported-precision":1,"inverted-revenue-ladder":1,"same-fact-two-homes":1,"unsupported-new-question":1,"same-passage-separate-records":1,"incorrect-ladder-arithmetic":1,"missing-direct-financial-evidence":1}}}